Unsupervised model evaluation

The evaluation package adds a read-only evaluation loop around the existing
deployed model. It does not retrain, recalibrate, update thresholds, write to the
outage table, or claim production accuracy without real incident labels.

```text
src/psap_kpi/evaluation/
├── evaluation_collector.py   # Chronological collection, replay, campaign, evidence files
├── production_scorer.py      # Pinned-artifact scoring with full denominator/per-head evidence
├── synthetic_faults.py       # Deterministic KPI injections and separate ground truth
├── model_health_check.py     # Pure PASS/WARN/FAIL/UNKNOWN checks and metrics
└── tests/                    # Focused offline tests
```

Method

1. Select an untouched chronological window strictly after the model’s training
and calibration cutoff.
2. Score every observed PSAP-hour with a pinned local copy of the deployed
artifact package and frozen thresholds.
3. Independently inject controlled scenarios into copies of representative
low-, medium-, and high-volume PSAP histories.
4. Score the exact untouched counterpart and injected version of every event
hour, retaining every candidate detector head.
5. Generate health evidence and synthetic-only precision/recall metrics.

The default campaign covers 396 independently isolated scenarios:

• Call-volume spikes and drops.
• Individual LSR, ASR, BID, and CSR degradation.
• Multi-KPI degradation.
• Mild, moderate, and severe changes.
• 1-, 2-, 3-, and 6-hour durations.
• Low-, medium-, and high-volume PSAPs.
• Slow-burn degradation, intermittent/flapping degradation, and correlated
call-volume plus multi-KPI failure.
• Benign success-rate improvements that should not increase a directional score.

CALL_VOLUME drops are intentionally retained as a challenge. The deployed
directional scorer treats positive volume residuals as bad and ignores negative
volume residuals, so the report exposes this blind spot separately.

Select exactly the scenarios to run

Without --scenario, the collector runs the full 396-scenario grid above. To
run exactly one test, add one self-contained --scenario option:

```powershell
python -m psap_kpi.evaluation.evaluation_collector `
  --input-csv C:\temp\psap_eval\untouched_hourly_kpis.csv `
  --run-dir C:\temp\psap-kpi\models\ae_cluster_runs\PINNED_RUN_ID `
  --training-cutoff-utc "2026-06-30 23:59:59Z" `
  --output-dir C:\temp\psap_eval\results `
  --scenario "pattern=kpi_degradation,kpis=ASR_SR,severity=severe,duration=3,volume=high"
```

That command runs exactly one severe, three-hour ASR degradation on a
high-volume PSAP. To run exactly two tests, repeat the option; each occurrence
may have its own pattern, KPIs, severity, duration, and volume stratum:

```powershell
python -m psap_kpi.evaluation.evaluation_collector `
  --input-csv C:\temp\psap_eval\untouched_hourly_kpis.csv `
  --run-dir C:\temp\psap-kpi\models\ae_cluster_runs\PINNED_RUN_ID `
  --training-cutoff-utc "2026-06-30 23:59:59Z" `
  --output-dir C:\temp\psap_eval\results `
  --scenario "pattern=volume_spike,severity=moderate,duration=1,volume=low" `
  --scenario "pattern=flapping,kpis=BID_SR+CSR_SR,severity=mild,duration=6,volume=medium"
```

Repeat --scenario any number of times. Valid patterns are volume_spike,
volume_drop, kpi_degradation, multi_kpi_degradation, slow_burn,
flapping, correlated_volume_sr, and benign_improvement. Severities are
mild, moderate, or severe; durations are 1, 2, 3, or 6 hours; volume
strata are low, medium, or high. Use + between multiple KPIs. Omitted
fields default to moderate severity and one hour; omitting volume allows the
injector to choose any volume stratum. --replicates must remain 1 when using
explicit scenarios; repeat the scenario option when another independent test
is wanted.

Run from an untouched CSV (PowerShell)

The CSV must contain one row per PSAP-hour with PSAP_ID, a timestamp named
HOUR_START_UTC or EVAL_TS_UTC, and CALL_VOLUME, LSR_SR, ASR_SR,
BID_SR, and CSR_SR.

```powershell
cd C:\temp\psap_kpi_evaluation_v1_1
$env:PYTHONPATH = "$PWD\src"

python -m psap_kpi.evaluation.evaluation_collector `
  --input-csv C:\temp\psap_eval\untouched_hourly_kpis.csv `
  --run-dir C:\temp\psap-kpi\models\ae_cluster_runs\PINNED_RUN_ID `
  --training-cutoff-utc "2026-06-30 23:59:59Z" `
  --output-dir C:\temp\psap_eval\results
```

Collect with the existing canonical Oracle loader

This route reuses psap_utils.queries.build_inference_sql; it does not create a
second KPI definition. Cache use is off by default for evaluation.

```powershell
python -m psap_kpi.evaluation.evaluation_collector `
  --oracle `
  --start-utc "2026-07-01 00:00:00Z" `
  --end-utc "2026-07-31 00:00:00Z" `
  --profile PRD `
  --market ALL `
  --run-dir C:\temp\psap-kpi\models\ae_cluster_runs\PINNED_RUN_ID `
  --training-cutoff-utc "2026-06-30 23:59:59Z" `
  --output-dir C:\temp\psap_eval\results
```

On later runs, add the previous baseline_scored_psap_hours.csv with
--reference-scored-csv to enable score/KPI drift by cluster, market, PSAP,
and weekday/weekend four-hour bucket.

Outputs

```text
baseline_scored_psap_hours.csv   # Every planned untouched row, including skips
paired_untouched_scored_psap_hours.csv # Exact untouched counterpart per event-hour
synthetic_scored_psap_hours.csv  # Every synthetic challenge row
per_head_score_evidence.csv      # Raw score, threshold, ratio, vote, availability
synthetic_row_truth.csv          # Row-level controlled ground truth
synthetic_event_truth.csv        # Event-level controlled ground truth
psap_model_health_evidence.json  # Checks, metrics, scope, model/data identity
```

The JSON reports controlled event/row detection, time to detection, score lift,
severity monotonicity, minimum detectable severity, temporal coverage, benign
controls, alert burden per 1,000 PSAP-hours, scoring/head/mapping coverage,
multi-head agreement and dispersion, score/threshold health, stability, and
optional reference drift. Baseline alert burden is explicitly a proxy—not a
false-positive rate—and synthetic precision/recall applies only to injected
ground truth.
